Article 11

Every Child has the following rights:

a. the right to live, grow and develop properly in accordance with human dignity;

b. to participate in all fields of life;

c. to obtain protection from acts of discrimination;

d. to obtain protection from economic and sexual exploitation;

e. to obtain protection from physical, psychological, sexual violence and neglect;

f. population identity and citizenship status;

g. to obtain a birth certificate;

h. to embrace religion and worship according to the teachings of religion and belief with the assistance of parental/guardian guidance;

i. not to be forced to change religion by foster parents, adoptive parents and by anyone;

j. to be recognized and know his/her parents, to be raised and cared for by his/her own parents;

k. to obtain health services and social security in accordance with physical, mental, spiritual, and social needs;

1. to obtain education and teaching in accordance with interests and talents;

m. to obtain care, education, training, self-improvement and ability to participate in community and state life for Children with physical, mental disabilities and special needs;

n. to express and have his/her opinion heard;

o. to rest and utilize free time for self-development outside school hours;

p. to obtain other rights in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

